WEBVTT

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:22.122
Though you are so close,
Kore hodo soba ni

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:26.626
I cannot tell you how I feel.
Iru no ni tsutaerarezu

00:00:26.626 --> 00:00:30.697
The more strongly I feel,
Tsuyoku omou hodo

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:35.301
the harder it is for me to find the words.
Kotoba ga mitsukaranai

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:43.343
What is sad is not fate...
Kanashii no wa unmei ja nakute

00:00:43.343 --> 00:00:54.117
...but that all encounters come to an end.
Deai no subete ni owari ga aru koto

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:58.558
O incomplete beings,
Mikan naru mono

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:02.996
awaken, for beyond the night...
mezameyo yoru o koetara

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:07.067
At the end of the desert...
Sabaku no hate ni

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:14.735
...the truth surely awaits you.
Shinjitsu ga matteru yo kitto

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:50.472
Oh, sorry! It's been so hectic around here.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:51.573
Not at all.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.902
It seems you had quite a time.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.715
It wasn't that big a deal.

00:01:55.715 --> 00:01:58.318
There just seem to be a lot of dangerous
characters running around.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.683
You are not going to rest yet?

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:03.214
Can't quite do that until
we find a safe camping site.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.751
After all, there might be
more of them on the way.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:08.828
Besides, I still have to do the
maintenance work on this guy.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:11.524
It's been tough, both here and there.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:15.427
Say, Iks, aren't you tired?

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:17.034
You can go ahead and go to sleep.

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.602
Right.

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.034
What the?

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.675
Where'd it go?

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.575
Oh, there it is!

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:30.880
Now then, shall we get you cleaned up, PSP?

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:37.521
Gravestone

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:40.524
Response is normal.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.261
Output stable and increasing.

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.498
Creation of a micro-wormhole confirmed.

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.632
What is the status of the wormhole?

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:48.756
It is still unstable.

00:02:49.536 --> 00:02:51.738
We do not have time. Hurry!

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:52.500
Yes, Ma'am!

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:55.335
Joganki.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.504
How are things going over there?

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:00.705
I've deployed the Inspection Force to Lutwik.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.008
If the worst happens, I'll have
them evacuate the residents.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.111
How are things with the wormhole driver?

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:09.351
There are some problems with it,

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:12.648
but I will have it ready to fire within a day or two.

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:15.591
I do not think we should be too hasty.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:17.552
We do not have time for that.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.330
The dome's rate of expansion is increasing.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.130
At this rate, even our
Hyperius may be in danger.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:25.271
That is exactly why.

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:29.742
It is not as if even we fully
understand the wormhole driver.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.107
The situation requires caution.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:34.640
The wormhole driver...

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:38.184
A weapon of destruction
that wipes out the target...

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:41.551
...by artificially creating
a distortion in space-time.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:46.520
Just like Gravestone, this weapon was
developed during the Great War,

00:03:46.826 --> 00:03:49.128
and The Third were putting all their resources...

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.460
...into their attempt to resurrect it.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:55.560
To think a time would come
to awaken such a thing...

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:57.330
We have no other choice.

00:03:57.604 --> 00:04:02.507
To rid this planet of any menace.
Is that not our duty as The Third?

00:04:04.577 --> 00:04:07.747
I will complete the wormhole driver without fail,

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:10.147
so that we may utterly destroy Gravestone.

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.581
Miss Honoka.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:54.960
Miss Honoka.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:58.029
Ouch!

00:04:58.731 --> 00:04:59.899
Are you all right?

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:03.801
I'm fine. I stopped myself just in time,
so I barely made contact.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.838
No, that's not what I meant.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:08.363
Whoa! I've sweated up a storm!

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:10.441
Bogie. Lights.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.078
Don't look.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:34.666
Is Miss Honoka not feeling well?

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:36.736
Yeah, it's happened again.

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.636
What do you mean, again?

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:40.540
She has nightmares every night.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.667
The circumstances are just as you saw.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:44.168
Bogie!

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.000
Miss Honoka.

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:48.474
It's nothing. Really.

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.878
Sometimes, I just don't sleep as well as I'd like.

00:05:51.017 --> 00:05:52.245
It's no big deal.

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:55.386
May we have a little talk?

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:56.750
What?

00:05:58.624 --> 00:06:00.023
What did you want to talk about?

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.962
Oh, is this about my health?!

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.097
If it's that, then I'm really fine...

00:06:04.097 --> 00:06:07.133
No, I will not deny that is part of it,

00:06:07.133 --> 00:06:10.236
but since my return, all
we've really said are our hellos...

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:12.136
...and we've not had a chance
to sit down and talk, so...

00:06:12.572 --> 00:06:14.073
We haven't?

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:17.600
But when you ask to talk to me so seriously...

00:06:18.044 --> 00:06:19.671
It doesn't matter what we talk about.

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:22.682
Perhaps, what happened during my absence?

00:06:22.682 --> 00:06:24.517
Is Millie well?

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:26.953
Yeah, she's doing good.

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:28.716
She's going to school.

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.584
Oh, a school is...

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:31.621
I know what that is.

00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:32.586
Okay.

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:37.196
She even said she'd made friends,
so she seems happy.

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:39.061
And Joey's working hard, too.

00:06:39.198 --> 00:06:42.827
As for Old Man Nor...
Well, we don't need to go there.

00:06:45.905 --> 00:06:46.894
What about you?

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:48.534
Did you finish your business?

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:49.470
Yes.

00:06:49.776 --> 00:06:51.778
I was wondering when you'd come back.

00:06:51.778 --> 00:06:53.143
I am sorry.

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.541
Then, you're back to stay for a while?

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:56.579
Yes.

00:06:57.517 --> 00:06:58.415
Okay.

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:02.653
There are still a lot of things I must see.

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:05.656
I will need you and Mr. Bogie to take me.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:07.684
Where?

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.154
Wherever.

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.286
The places you know.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:13.291
The places you do not know.

00:07:13.633 --> 00:07:16.932
The places in this world which I must see.

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:21.698
But...

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:23.838
...when you're done with that...

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.172
Someday...

00:07:26.078 --> 00:07:27.739
It's bad timing.

00:07:28.014 --> 00:07:28.912
What?

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:30.583
Knowing you,

00:07:30.583 --> 00:07:34.178
couldn't you have figured out
that I was with someone else?

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:37.188
You didn't have to make it tonight, of all nights.

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:43.189
Just kidding!

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:45.264
Come on, let's go to sleep already.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.526
We've got an early start tomorrow, too.

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:50.124
Man, I wonder if Teacher will wake
up when she's supposed to.

00:07:50.470 --> 00:07:51.528
Miss Honoka.

00:07:52.605 --> 00:07:55.808
I returned tonight for a reason.

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:56.900
Huh? What reason?

00:07:57.643 --> 00:08:01.409
Would it be possible for you to turn back?

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.116
I'm on a job.

00:08:21.601 --> 00:08:23.569
The magnetic field of sand dragons, huh?

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:29.671
Teacher...

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:31.532
Sorry!

00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:02.139
This is...

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:07.679
Good morning.

00:09:33.239 --> 00:09:34.540
Magnetic field confirmed.

00:09:34.540 --> 00:09:36.235
It's definitely a trace left
behind by sand dragons.

00:09:36.642 --> 00:09:39.076
Looks like we're going in the right direction.

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:42.239
Yes, but the magnetic field
has grown quite weak.

00:09:42.481 --> 00:09:45.712
At this rate, it might become
undetectable soon.

00:09:46.319 --> 00:09:47.411
Don't worry.

00:09:48.688 --> 00:09:52.146
The direction we should go... I think I can tell.

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:53.883
What do you mean you can tell?

00:09:54.427 --> 00:09:57.225
The reason she had declined
Iks' proposal to turn back...

00:09:57.730 --> 00:10:00.631
...was not only out of her
usual sense of professionalism.

00:10:02.868 --> 00:10:05.972
The odd sensation on her
forehead and her unease...

00:10:05.972 --> 00:10:08.702
...were gradually growing more concrete.

00:10:09.342 --> 00:10:11.742
It was as if someone were
waiting for her up ahead.

00:10:12.111 --> 00:10:15.376
A strange sensation that someone
was calling to her from somewhere.

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:17.381
That was what Honoka felt.

00:10:27.693 --> 00:10:28.751
Miss Honoka...

00:11:02.728 --> 00:11:03.251
What is it?

00:11:05.698 --> 00:11:06.494
What?!

00:11:13.039 --> 00:11:15.200
It's no use. I'm getting no reading.

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:18.340
It seems the magnetic field has vanished.

00:11:18.644 --> 00:11:21.213
Honoka said she could tell the direction,

00:11:21.213 --> 00:11:22.942
but what did she mean by that?

00:11:57.983 --> 00:12:00.349
She's acting a little strange.

00:12:01.687 --> 00:12:03.086
It isn't like her.

00:12:03.589 --> 00:12:05.091
Did something happen?

00:12:05.091 --> 00:12:06.992
Don't talk to me so familiarly.

00:12:06.992 --> 00:12:07.515
What?

00:12:08.094 --> 00:12:11.029
I haven't decided if I trust you yet.

00:12:11.797 --> 00:12:14.561
Though, I've kept quiet,
since Hono seems to trust you.

00:12:15.201 --> 00:12:18.136
You must trust Miss Honoka then.

00:12:21.373 --> 00:12:22.237
Bogie.

00:12:22.575 --> 00:12:23.439
What is it?

00:12:23.642 --> 00:12:25.667
This is just my hunch, but...

00:12:26.345 --> 00:12:28.643
Was that the first time
she cut down a person?

00:12:30.182 --> 00:12:32.118
No, that was not the first time.

00:12:32.118 --> 00:12:34.153
I didn't phrase that well.

00:12:34.153 --> 00:12:36.644
Wasn't that the first time she'd
killed someone with her sword?

00:12:36.856 --> 00:12:37.914
You're right.

00:12:37.990 --> 00:12:42.120
As far as I know, Honoka has never
killed another person with her sword.

00:12:42.828 --> 00:12:44.625
Excluding last night's incident.

00:12:46.999 --> 00:12:48.432
I thought as much.

00:12:48.834 --> 00:12:50.096
Stupid girl.

00:12:54.039 --> 00:12:55.131
Miss Honoka...

00:13:12.858 --> 00:13:13.950
Teacher.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.225
Is something the matter?

00:13:16.295 --> 00:13:18.264
Something's the matter with you!

00:13:18.264 --> 00:13:18.696
What?

00:13:19.331 --> 00:13:21.094
Do you know what that guy said?

00:13:21.233 --> 00:13:22.268
That guy?

00:13:22.268 --> 00:13:23.469
That man.

00:13:23.469 --> 00:13:25.704
The spacey one with the silly
smile plastered on his face,

00:13:25.704 --> 00:13:27.069
whose true identity is unknown!

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.071
Is something the matter with Iks?

00:13:30.776 --> 00:13:32.266
"It isn't like her."

00:13:32.678 --> 00:13:34.145
That's what he said.

00:13:34.647 --> 00:13:36.239
"It isn't like her."

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:40.082
Why does he have the right
to say something like that?!

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:42.444
Teacher, could it be...

00:13:43.155 --> 00:13:43.678
What?!

00:13:44.123 --> 00:13:46.921
...that you hate men?

00:13:47.126 --> 00:13:48.127
I detest them!

00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:50.095
But he's not a bad person...

00:13:50.095 --> 00:13:51.687
I don't care about him!

00:13:53.499 --> 00:13:54.727
You're scared, aren't you?

00:14:01.674 --> 00:14:04.973
That's why you're so flustered and
huddled in on yourself, isn't it?

00:14:05.477 --> 00:14:07.240
Because you don't know what to do.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.941
Does it look that way?

00:14:10.149 --> 00:14:12.083
It does. It's so stupid.

00:14:12.918 --> 00:14:14.613
Just because you cut down a person...

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.784
Just because you killed a person,
what're you all depressed for?!

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:20.522
Even if you hadn't killed him, I would've.

00:14:20.759 --> 00:14:23.592
You kill or be killed.
That's the way of the world.

00:14:24.296 --> 00:14:25.593
You should know that, too!

00:14:27.633 --> 00:14:29.191
Carefully recall what happened!

00:14:32.171 --> 00:14:34.773
I'm the one who first shot him.

00:14:34.773 --> 00:14:36.741
I'm also the one who finished him off.

00:14:37.042 --> 00:14:38.878
I'm a killer.

00:14:38.878 --> 00:14:40.646
Something like that is no big deal.

00:14:40.646 --> 00:14:42.011
You can't mean that!

00:14:43.115 --> 00:14:45.451
If you knew of the things I've done in the past,

00:14:45.451 --> 00:14:46.509
you'd probably regret what you did.

00:14:47.419 --> 00:14:50.115
You would think that you shouldn't
have saved a woman like me!

00:14:50.656 --> 00:14:52.157
That's not true!

00:14:52.157 --> 00:14:54.091
Besides, cutting down that person...

00:14:55.261 --> 00:14:58.628
It's not that I regret cutting down that man.

00:14:59.164 --> 00:15:00.324
Then what is it?

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:03.295
It's not as if he was the first.

00:15:03.535 --> 00:15:06.197
Ants, lizards, autonomous soldiers...

00:15:06.372 --> 00:15:08.363
I've cut down various things in the past.

00:15:09.275 --> 00:15:10.105
Autonomous soldiers?

00:15:10.943 --> 00:15:14.179
I've never turned my sword on
anything unless I was dead serious.

00:15:14.179 --> 00:15:17.046
Just as you said, kill or be killed.

00:15:17.249 --> 00:15:19.274
I drew my sword only because I believed that.

00:15:19.685 --> 00:15:22.916
Even now, I don't think that my
judgment in doing so was wrong.

00:15:23.889 --> 00:15:24.548
But...

00:15:25.591 --> 00:15:27.422
The sensation remains with me.

00:15:27.993 --> 00:15:30.896
When I remember, I feel ill
and I want to throw up.

00:15:30.896 --> 00:15:33.626
But that's strange, isn't it?

00:15:33.766 --> 00:15:35.701
Just because my opponent was a human?

00:15:35.701 --> 00:15:38.103
As long as my own motivation is unchanged,

00:15:38.103 --> 00:15:40.264
things should be the same,
no matter what my opponent is.

00:15:42.875 --> 00:15:45.878
I wonder if I'm a hypocrite...

00:15:45.878 --> 00:15:46.970
This is garbage!

00:15:47.079 --> 00:15:48.047
What?

00:15:48.047 --> 00:15:51.216
Don't talk to me about something
you could say to anyone!

00:15:51.216 --> 00:15:54.481
Please! I'm begging you! Don't disappoint me!

00:15:55.354 --> 00:15:55.979
Liar!

00:15:56.588 --> 00:15:57.452
Teacher?

00:16:03.495 --> 00:16:06.794
Oh man. You're faster than me.

00:16:09.234 --> 00:16:10.269
This time, we do this barehanded.

00:16:10.269 --> 00:16:10.735
What?

00:16:23.549 --> 00:16:24.607
Strike back at me!

00:16:24.817 --> 00:16:26.114
What's wrong, Honoka?!

00:16:39.431 --> 00:16:42.093
Her techniques were ineffective against Honoka.

00:16:42.634 --> 00:16:45.068
Paife was certain of that.

00:16:46.005 --> 00:16:50.066
Right then, she was not trying
to land a blow on Honoka.

00:16:50.909 --> 00:16:55.471
She was trying to set a certain
trap that was not a direct attack.

00:16:56.248 --> 00:16:57.442
However...

00:17:05.124 --> 00:17:06.250
I can't win...

00:17:28.047 --> 00:17:29.480
That worked up a good sweat.

00:17:30.049 --> 00:17:32.210
If you're that energetic, you should be fine.

00:17:40.025 --> 00:17:41.151
Teacher...

00:17:45.197 --> 00:17:46.391
Good work out there.

00:17:51.136 --> 00:17:52.125
Were you serious?

00:17:53.906 --> 00:17:55.373
Yes, I was serious.

00:17:55.874 --> 00:17:58.775
I fought seriously, like I was trying to kill her.

00:17:59.511 --> 00:18:00.569
But...

00:18:03.715 --> 00:18:05.842
That girl's a monster.

00:18:28.107 --> 00:18:28.505
Oh...

00:18:29.108 --> 00:18:30.507
Good morning!

00:18:32.077 --> 00:18:32.736
Morning.

00:18:41.186 --> 00:18:43.620
The trap Paife had tried to set...

00:18:43.789 --> 00:18:46.952
It was a certain technique that involved chi.

00:18:47.693 --> 00:18:51.322
However, it was also ineffective against Honoka.

00:18:52.931 --> 00:18:56.332
The magnetic field left by the sand
dragons had completely disappeared.

00:18:57.236 --> 00:19:02.071
Having lost the trail,
it was Honoka who led the party.

00:19:05.077 --> 00:19:07.012
Are we really doing okay?

00:19:07.012 --> 00:19:10.743
Yes. Please just follow what Miss Honoka says.

00:19:12.651 --> 00:19:13.982
What's going on here?

00:19:15.821 --> 00:19:16.480
It's close.

00:19:18.056 --> 00:19:19.318
Over here?

00:19:20.125 --> 00:19:23.151
Activating the final countdown process.

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:26.222
Commencing final countdown!

00:19:43.882 --> 00:19:44.849
Thank you for your hard work.

00:19:45.651 --> 00:19:46.948
To you as well.

00:19:47.319 --> 00:19:50.982
The wormhole driver has
begun the final countdown.

00:19:51.256 --> 00:19:54.157
It is slated to attack the target in 6 hours.

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:58.291
It is a wonder that we have managed
to get this far in such a short time.

00:19:58.497 --> 00:19:59.088
Indeed.

00:20:00.065 --> 00:20:02.898
But this is not over yet.

00:20:03.135 --> 00:20:07.128
Will the wormhole driver
work as we expect it to?

00:20:09.474 --> 00:20:10.338
Joganki.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:14.840
There is something I believe you should know.

00:20:19.051 --> 00:20:22.077
He has been sighted in the
vicinity of the distortion field.

00:20:22.788 --> 00:20:23.720
He?

00:20:24.389 --> 00:20:27.051
I see. It is not inconceivable.

00:20:27.159 --> 00:20:29.457
He must be interested in what is happening...

00:20:29.962 --> 00:20:30.451
Wait!

00:20:31.096 --> 00:20:32.688
He is there? Then...

00:20:33.198 --> 00:20:35.462
She is also... Honoka is also with him.

00:20:51.516 --> 00:20:52.813
Why did you not report this to me?

00:20:53.452 --> 00:20:55.454
What would be the point in reporting it?

00:20:55.454 --> 00:20:58.184
We cannot change our plans for her alone.

00:20:58.724 --> 00:21:01.293
When the wormhole driver fires,

00:21:01.293 --> 00:21:02.894
not only will it take out Gravestone,

00:21:02.894 --> 00:21:04.691
but it will completely destroy
the land around it as well.

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:08.931
The probability of any life
surviving is likely close to zero.

00:21:10.702 --> 00:21:11.964
Honoka...

00:21:45.070 --> 00:21:48.073
A flexible civilization...
Juunan na bunmei wa

00:21:48.073 --> 00:21:50.575
...is always rapidly advancing.
Itsudatte nisshin-geppo

00:21:50.575 --> 00:21:53.545
You and your dreams are also...
Kimi to yume mo

00:21:53.545 --> 00:21:57.345
...making headway even now.
Genzai shinkou

00:22:02.888 --> 00:22:05.857
I realized for the first time...
Hajimete kizuitan da

00:22:05.857 --> 00:22:09.554
...with that line, resembling a surprise attack.
Fui-uchi ni nita sono serifu de

00:22:14.599 --> 00:22:17.536
My sixth sense was pried open.
Kojiakerareta dai-rokkan

00:22:17.536 --> 00:22:21.563
I'd been waiting for this feeling this whole time.
Kono kankaku o zutto matteita

00:22:25.577 --> 00:22:28.547
Opening my heart, just opening it...
Kokoro o hiraite tada hiraite

00:22:28.547 --> 00:22:31.516
I embrace the voices of strangers.
Daisansha no koe ukeireru

00:22:31.516 --> 00:22:34.386
Earnestly persevering, just persevering...
Hitasura koraete tada koraete

00:22:34.386 --> 00:22:37.480
I even try turning pages of criticism.
Hinan no peeji mo aketemiru

00:22:37.789 --> 00:22:40.759
I'm going to leave my...
Toushindai no boku wa

00:22:40.759 --> 00:22:43.626
...true-to-life self behind, right here.
Koko ni oite iku yo

00:22:43.695 --> 00:22:47.499
You can say whatever you want now...
Mou nanto itte kuretemo

00:22:47.499 --> 00:22:49.023
...and I'm fine with that.
Kekkou da

00:22:49.534 --> 00:22:55.006
Ah, how simple is the impulse to evolve.
Aa nante tanjun da shinka shitai to iu shoudou

00:22:55.006 --> 00:22:57.943
You and your dreams are also...
Kimi to yume mo

00:22:57.943 --> 00:23:01.140
...making headway even now.
Genzai shinkou

00:23:15.160 --> 00:23:16.889
Preview

00:23:17.162 --> 00:23:19.255
What awaited us at the end of the desert...

00:23:19.364 --> 00:23:22.299
...was the super weapon, Gravestone,
awakened from its slumber.

00:23:22.534 --> 00:23:25.370
As we walked into it, what awaited us there...

00:23:25.370 --> 00:23:27.600
...was the horrific Great War of the past.

00:23:27.973 --> 00:23:29.441
We were assaulted by a sudden bombardment...

00:23:29.441 --> 00:23:32.535
...and a flash of light that
bathed everything in sight.

00:23:32.644 --> 00:23:36.546
Facing this tremendously large explosion, I...

00:23:37.282 --> 00:23:40.552
Next time on
The Third - The Girl With The Blue Eye,

00:23:40.552 --> 00:23:42.053
episode 11, "Battling Against Illusion".

00:23:42.053 --> 00:23:43.422
Battling Against Illusion
episode 11, "Battling Against Illusion".

00:23:43.422 --> 00:23:44.912
Battling Against Illusion
